{"id":"o-fws-gov","title":"Havasu National Wildlife Refuge","cat":"water","art":"cruise","area":"Topock, AZ","metroId":"denver","src":"fws.gov","rating":4.7,"reviews":1239,"specs":["318 bird species rely on the diverse habitat","Wildlife includes coyotes, foxes, bobcats, desert bighorn, mountain lions, and bats","20-mile Topock Gorge is one of the last remaining natural stretches of the river"],"options":[{"name":"Fishing Tips","detail":"","price":null},{"name":"Surf and wake","detail":"","price":null},{"name":"Guided Tours","detail":"2 hours (9 to 11 am)","price":null}],"services":[{"name":"Fishing Tips","desc":"Purchasing a fishing license directly contributes to conservation efforts. License fees provide critical funding for state fish and wildlife agencies and are one part of the broader funding system that supports conservation and outdoor access across the country. Each year, our Sport Fish Restoration Program apportions","photo":"https://www.fws.gov/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fdoifwsnextprod.prod.acquia-sites.com%2Fsites%2Fdefault%2Ffiles%2Fstyles%2Fratio_3x4%2Fpublic%2F2022-02%2FCarson%2520NFH%2520pc%2520Cheri%2520Anderson.jpg.webp%3Fh%3D7685ba0d%26itok%3Dzfbsh5se&w=3840&q=75","variants":[{"label":"Standard","price":null,"optionIdx":0}]},{"name":"Surf and wake","desc":null,"variants":[{"label":"Standard","price":null,"optionIdx":1}]},{"name":"Guided Tours","desc":null,"variants":[{"label":"2 hours (9 to 11 am)","price":null,"optionIdx":2}]}],"includes":["Guided tour with information about plants, animals, and conservation efforts"],"addons":[],"gap":"Price for guided tours not stated","blurb":"Havasu National Wildlife Refuge was established in 1941 to provide migratory bird habitat. Visitors can enjoy boating through Topock Gorge, fishing in Topock Marsh, and hiking in the Havasu Wilderness Area. Guided tours are offered monthly from November to April, focusing on local plants, animals, and conservation efforts.","cover":"https://www.fws.gov/sites/default/